`bun-test-utils` and every package in this workspace are dual-licensed under
either of:

- **Apache License, Version 2.0** — [`LICENSE-APACHE`](./LICENSE-APACHE)
  ([spdx: Apache-2.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/Apache-2.0.html))
- **MIT License** — [`LICENSE-MIT`](./LICENSE-MIT)
  ([spdx: MIT](https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html))

at your option. The SPDX expression for this is `MIT OR Apache-2.0`.

You may use this software under the terms of *either* licence. You do not have
to comply with both. Pick whichever fits your project and keep the
corresponding notice.

## Why both

This is the same arrangement the Rust ecosystem settled on. MIT is short,
permissive, and universally understood; Apache-2.0 adds an explicit patent
grant and a patent-retaliation clause that some organisations require before
they can take a dependency. Offering both means neither constituency has to
negotiate.

## Contribution

